hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15519","Bahz and Affan both said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Yala ibn Ata, from al-Walid ibn Abd al-Rahman, from al-Harith ibn Abdullah ibn Aws al-Thaqafi, he said: I asked Umar ibn al-Khattab about a woman who performs tawaf of the House then menstruates, he said: Let the last of her contact be the tawaf of the House, so al-Harith said: Thus the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me fatwa, so Umar, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, said: You rendered from your hands, you asked me about something you had asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about, but I do not oppose."
"15520","Ahmad ibn al-Hajjaj and Ali ibn Ishaq both said: Abdullah informed us, he said: al-Hajjaj ibn Artah informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn al-Mughirah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Baylamani, from Amr ibn Aws, from al-Harith ibn Abdullah ibn Aws, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs Hajj of the House or Umrah, let the last of his contact be with the House. So his hadith reached Umar, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, and he said to him: You slipped out of your hands, did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and not inform us of it."
"15521","Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, he said: Abbad informed us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Abd al-Malik ibn al-Mughirah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Baylamani, from Amr ibn Aws, from al-Harith ibn Aws, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs Hajj or Umrah, let the last of his contact be the tawaf of the House. So Umar ibn al-Khattab said to him: You slipped out of your hands, you heard this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) then you did not narrate it to me."
